    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## 2. Gamma Distribution MLE [S+N]\n\nFor the Gamma distribution with shape $\\alpha$ and rate $\\beta$:\n$$f(x; \\alpha, \\beta) = \\frac{\\beta^\\alpha}{\\Gamma(\\alpha)} x^{\\alpha-1} e^{-\\beta x}$$\n\nThe log-likelihood per observation is\n$$\\ell_i(\\alpha, \\beta) = \\alpha \\ln\\beta - \\ln\\Gamma(\\alpha) + (\\alpha-1)\\ln x_i - \\beta x_i$$\n\nThere is no closed-form MLE for $\\alpha$. The score involves the digamma function $\\psi(\\alpha)$, which is not available as an array operation — so we use finite-difference gradient approximation.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* Symbolic log-likelihood for Gamma */\nll_gamma_i(alpha, beta, x_i) := alpha*log(beta) - log(gamma(alpha))\n  + (alpha - 1)*log(x_i) - beta*x_i$\n\n/* Score function */\nscore_gamma_alpha : diff(ll_gamma_i(alpha, beta, x[i]), alpha);\nscore_gamma_beta : diff(ll_gamma_i(alpha, beta, x[i]), beta);",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "log(beta)+log(x[i])-psi[0](alpha)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "{{\\alpha}\\over{\\beta}}-x_{i}"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 5,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The $\\alpha$-score involves $\\psi(\\alpha) = \\frac{d}{d\\alpha}\\ln\\Gamma(\\alpha)$ (digamma function). Since we lack an array-level digamma, we use central finite differences for the gradient.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* Finite-difference gradient helper */\nfd_gradient(f, x, eps) := block([nd, g],\n  nd : np_size(x), g : np_zeros([nd]),\n  for j : 0 thru nd - 1 do block([xp, xm],\n    xp : np_copy(x), np_set(xp, j, np_ref(x, j) + eps),\n    xm : np_copy(x), np_set(xm, j, np_ref(x, j) - eps),\n    np_set(g, j, (f(xp) - f(xm)) / (2 * eps))),\n  g)$\n\n/* Generate Gamma(3, 2) data via sum-of-exponentials */\nn_gam : 300$\ndata_gam : np_zeros([n_gam])$\nfor k : 1 thru 3 do\n  data_gam : np_add(data_gam,\n    np_scale(0.5, np_neg(np_log(np_rand([n_gam])))))$\n\n/* NLL with log-transforms for positivity */\nnll_gam(p) := block([a, b, sum_log, sum_x],\n  a : exp(np_ref(p, 0)),\n  b : exp(np_ref(p, 1)),\n  sum_log : np_sum(np_log(data_gam)),\n  sum_x : np_sum(data_gam),\n  -(n_gam * (a*log(b) - log(gamma(a))) + (a - 1)*sum_log - b*sum_x))$\n\nnll_gam_grad(p) := fd_gradient(nll_gam, p, 1e-5)$\n\n[p_gam, _, _] : np_minimize(nll_gam, nll_gam_grad,\n  ndarray([0.5, 0.5]), 1e-8, 200)$\nprint(\"Fitted: alpha =\", exp(np_ref(p_gam, 0)),\n      \", beta =\", exp(np_ref(p_gam, 1)))$\nprint(\"True:   alpha = 3, beta = 2\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Fitted: alpha = 3.0721177499279255 , beta = 2.093281370724017\nTrue:   alpha = 3, beta = 2"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ax_draw2d(\n  color=\"steelblue\",\n  ax_histogram(np_to_list(data_gam)),\n  title=\"Gamma MLE: Histogram of Data\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"Count\", grid=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
